Build storage key paths with backslashes on every platform.

THierarchicalStorage joins registry and INI key paths (Sessions\My site)
through its IncludeTrailingBackslash and ExcludeTrailingBackslash members,
which defer to the RTL functions of those names. The RTL's add and strip the
platform's path delimiter: a backslash on Windows, a slash on POSIX, where
these functions also build local file paths. Keys are not file paths: their
separator is a backslash everywhere, and the INI file's sections say so. The
members now add and strip a backslash themselves; on Windows that is what
the RTL did, so upstream's behaviour is unchanged. Without this, on POSIX
the current key became "Sessions/", matched no section, and no stored site
loaded. Line counts are unchanged.

--- a/source/core/HierarchicalStorage.cpp	2026-10-11 20:24:50.370319077 -0300
+++ b/source/core/HierarchicalStorage.cpp	2026-10-11 20:24:50.391977479 -0300
@@ -896,7 +896,7 @@
   }
   else
   {
-    return ::IncludeTrailingBackslash(S);
+    if (S[S.Length()] == L'\\') { return S; } return S + L'\\'; // linscp: keys use backslashes on any platform
   }
 }
 //---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@ -909,7 +909,7 @@
   }
   else
   {
-    return ::ExcludeTrailingBackslash(S);
+    if (S[S.Length()] == L'\\') { return S.SubString(1, S.Length() - 1); } return S; // linscp: as above
   }
 }
 //---------------------------------------------------------------------------
